  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LPI Inclusive Peace in Practice 2018-2023 - Life and Peace Institute global policy</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">LPI Inclusive Peace in Practice 2018-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Initiativet Inclusive Peace in Practice 2018-2022 av the Life &amp; Peace Institute (LPI) fokuserar fr&#xe4;mst p&#xe5; att f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndra lokala-till-globala engagemang kring globala fredsbyggande policies och normer, som till exempel Sustaining Peace Agenda, diskursen kring Youth, Peace and Security (YPS) och Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), och p&#xe5; att fr&#xe4;mja st&#xf6;rre grad av inkludering i relevanta policyprocesser. Det drivs av tron p&#xe5; att mer j&#xe4;mlikhet, deltagande och reciprocitet mellan globala beslutsfattare och lokala akt&#xf6;rer kan &#xe4;ndra normer &#xf6;ver tid och d&#xe4;rmed fr&#xe4;mja fredsbyggande policies som &#xe4;r mer anpassade till den dagliga verkligheten i konfliktdrabbade omr&#xe5;den, och d&#xe4;rmed mer effektiva och mer h&#xe5;llbara. Ett centralt fokus, givet LPI:s engagemang i typiskt sv&#xe5;r&#xe5;tkomna omr&#xe5;den, &#xe4;r att p&#xe5;verka policies i st&#xe4;ngda, os&#xe4;kra och informella milj&#xf6;er. LPI drar &#xe4;ven p&#xe5; sina partnerskap, erfarenheter fr&#xe5;n landprogrammen och sina bepr&#xf6;vade metoder som till exempel ledsagande-modellen och Participatory Action Research-ansatsen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Inclusive Peace in Practice initiative 2018-2022 by the Life &amp; Peace Institute (LPI) focuses primarily on how to transform the local-to-global engagement on global peacebuilding policies and norms, such as the Sustaining Peace Agenda, the Youth, Peace and Security (YPS) discourse and the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), and to promote inclusion in relevant policy processes. It is driven by the belief that greater equity, participation, and reciprocity between global decision-makers and local actors can shift norms over time and foster peacebuilding policy that is more directly connected to day-to-day lives in conflict affected areas, and thus more effective and more sustainable. A key focus, given LPI&apos;s engagement in typical &apos;hard-to-reach&apos; areas, is policy-influencing in closed, insecure and informal environments. LPI furthermore draws on its partnerships, experiences from country programmes and its tested methodologies such as the accompaniment model and the Participatory Action Research approach.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of the Inclusive Peace in Practice (IPIP) initiative for the period until December 2023 is:
Key actors within the peacebuilding ecosystem collaborate more effectively to develop and realise transformative global policy responses to specific conflicts

The Life and Peace Institute (LPI) stresses that the goal statement reflects the systems change that IPIP, along with others in the peacebuilding ecosystem, will work towards within the next 10 to 20 years. Key actors within the system are individuals and institutions whose efforts are relevant to specific conflict situations  from local peace activists, civil society organisations, national authorities to international NGOs, think tanks and academic institutions, global networks and regional and global policy actors. Ultimately, it is LPI&apos;s vision that this change is meant to be felt positively by women, men, young women, young men, girls and boys living in violent conflict-affected contexts.</narrative>
  </description>
